<title>FINLAND: AKTIA Q1 OPERATING PROFIT DOUBLES TO FIM 12.7 MLN.</title>
<headline>AKTIA Q1 OPERATING PROFIT DOUBLES TO FIM 12.7 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>				     (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit after credit losses	12.7 vs 5.7</p>
<p> Loan and guarantee losses		     13.1 vs 13.9</p>
<p> Net income from financial operations	69.1 vs 62.5</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   0.36 vs 0.27</p>
<p> Capital adequacy (BIS) (percent)	    13.1 vs 9.6</p>
<p> Income to expenses ratio			1.36 vs 1.26</p>
<p> Interest income				  120.2 vs 126.8</p>
<p> Interest expenses				 51.1 vs 64.3</p>
<p> NET INCOME FROM FINANCIAL OPERATIONS	69.1 vs 62.5</p>
<p> Dividend income				    0.2 vs 0.1</p>
<p> Commission income				 28.5 vs 25.2</p>
<p>Net income from securities transactions</p>
<p> and forex dealings			  loss 1.2 vs 2.7 profit</p>
<p> Other operating income			  17.7 vs 18.5</p>
<p> TOTAL INCOME				     114.3 vs 109.0</p>
<p> Personnel expenses				37.7 vs 33.8</p>
<p> Other administrative expenses		 22.4 vs 18.8</p>
<p> Depreciation					 6.6 vs 6.9</p>
<p> Other operating expenses			17.5 vs 27.1</p>
<p> TOTAL EXPENSES				    84.2 vs 86.6</p>
<p> Loan and guarantee losses		     13.1 vs 13.9</p>
<p> Write-downs on securities			5.0 vs 3.7</p>
<p> Share of associated companies profits	0.7 vs 0.9</p>
<p> PROFIT ON ORDINARY OPERATIONS		 12.7 vs 5.7</p>
<p> Extraordinary items, taxes	    charge 1.1 vs 1.0 gain</p>
<p> NET PROFIT					   11.6 vs 6.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the Finnish banking group is Aktia</p>
<p>Saastopankki Oy.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248, news@reuters.fi</p>
